'checkin:Send a snapshot checkout'\''s branches back to the server, grafted onto its real history' \
'integrate:Merge a branch into the server'\''s target branch (checking it in first), then refresh this checkout' \
'slice:Named sets of paths to check out together, kept on the server'\''s target branch' \
'clone:Copy a remote repository into a new directory' \
'remote:List remotes, or add one' \
'log:Show recent commits reachable from HEAD' \
'revs:List or count commits matching revision ranges' \
'merge-base:Find merge bases or test whether one commit is an ancestor of another' \
'reflog:Show, delete, or expire reflog entries' \
'blame:Show who last modified each line of a file' \
'diff:Show changes as a diff. No argument\: uncommitted changes; with a commit\: the change that commit introduced; with two commits (or \`A..B\`) diff their trees' \
'show:Show information about a commit, tag, or branch (defaults to HEAD)' \
'status:Show what'\''s changed and where you are (this is the default)' \
'shortlog:List the commits on this branch that aren'\''t on the target branch yet' \
'ahead:List the commits on this branch that aren'\''t on the target branch yet' \
'add:Stage changes. With no paths, stages everything' \
'rm:Remove tracked paths from the working tree and index' \
'mv:Rename or move tracked paths' \
'clean:Remove untracked files from the working tree' \
'repack:Pack reachable objects and remove redundant packs' \
'gc:Pack refs, expire reflogs, repack, prune, and refresh commit-graph' \
'fsck:Check refs, objects, and pack indexes for problems' \
'ignore:Query exclude (gitignore) rules' \
'hooks:List hook scripts or run one by name' \
'patch-id:Print stable patch-IDs for commits or revision ranges' \
'resolve:Resolve revision specs to object ids and types' \
'cat:Show blob, tree, commit, or tag contents for a revision spec' \
'commit:Stage every change and record a new commit' \
'branch:List branches, or create / delete / rename / configure one' \
'switch:Switch to another branch, remote branch, or detached commit' \
'reset:Move the branch tip and optionally reset the index or worktree' \
'merge:Merge another branch, tag or commit into the current branch' \
'pick:Cherry-pick commits onto the current branch' \
'revert:Undo commits with new inverse commits' \
'history:Rewrite commits without a sequencer (plan, then apply refs atomically)' \
'stash:Save or restore shelved work' \
'restore:Restore working tree and/or index paths' \
'fetch:Download refs and objects from a remote' \
'pull:Fetch from the remote and integrate it into the current branch' \
'rebase:Replay local commits onto a new base (atomic ref update)' \
'push:Publish refs to a remote' \
'bundle:Create, verify, or list git bundle files' \
'notes:List, show, add, or remove Git notes on commits' \
'tag:List tags, or create / delete one' \
'worktree:List, add, or remove linked worktrees' \
'auth:Sign in to grithub (GitHub inside a github.com repository), a \`grit serve\` host, or store a username and token for any HTTPS host' \
'login:Sign in to grithub (GitHub inside a github.com repository), a \`grit serve\` host, or store a username and token for any HTTPS host' \
'update:Update grit to the latest release (re-runs the install script)' \
'skill:Print an agent skill (SKILL.md) that explains how to use grit' \
'completions:Generate shell completion scripts for bash, zsh, or fish' \
'config:Read, set, or list configuration values' \
'manager:Git credential helper backed by the Windows Credential Manager' \
'serve:Serve repositories over HTTP, with a web view where people sign in with email and password' \
'upload-pack:Serve a fetch or clone over stdin/stdout (run by ssh and grit-http-server)' \
'receive-pack:Accept a push over stdin/stdout (run by ssh and grit-http-server)' \
